6.208.m:
The brāhmaṇa said:
"First I went from the hermitage to Avantī, the city of Hari;
from there, having bathed in the waters of the Somodbhavā, I went to Dvārakā.

6.209.m:
The servant-girl said:
"O master, my lord was killed in the night by some thief;
the jewelry and fine silk garments of his daughter-in-law were taken entirely.

6.210.m:
Mukunda said:
"I will tell you, O guru, what happened after death;
by the grace of this sacred place, memory now arises in me.

6.212.m:
And he spoke to that fortunate twice-born who desired liberation.
Viṣṇu said:
O twice-born, this Indraprastha is the highest among all sacred fords, / just as Śambhu is among all knowers of Brahman, just as the river Gaṅgā is among rivers;
